otect the work of creators.", "type": ""}}, {"content": "secondary_8", "type": "objective"}], "id": 1}, {"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 0, "selected": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "to be influenced", "type": "text"}], "id": 1, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn10le12ob07re6aud08", "type": "audio"}, {"content": "It is acceptable", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"content": "by a work of art, but you have to be careful.", "type": ""}}, {"content": "secondary_8", "type": "objective"}], "id": 2}, {"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 0, "selected": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "If you mimic", "type": "text"}], "id": 1, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn10le12ob07re6aud09", "type": "audio"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "post_question", "contents": {"content": "an original piece of work too closely, you can be accused of being a copycat.", "type": ""}}, {"content": "secondary_8", "type": "objective"}], "id": 3}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nGail talks about copyright and other work issues.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: <span class=\"bullet\">Listen to the audio. <span class=\"bullet\">Type in the missing words. <span class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}], "id": 9, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "RSLT", "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 0, "selected": 0}, {"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 1, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Quiz", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}], "id": 10, "stimuli_ids": []}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "DWS", "questions": [{"responses": [{"_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "id": 0, "correct": 1, "selected": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "engenn10le12ob07re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " \nShare your opinion about an important work related matter.\n", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "id": 1, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le12ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le12ob07re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"image": "engenn10le12ob07re2img05.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn10le12ob07re2img05.jpg", "text": "Being pressured to meet a deadline may cause some employees to borrow and present another person's thoughts or  ideas as their own. It is seen as a quick and easy way to be done with their work. This work \"borrowing\" is also known as plagiarism. You may wonder, \"How do people do such things?\" It shouldn't be allowed and it isn't, but it happens more often than you think.", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn10le12ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "You usually think of plagiarism as writers' stories  having been stolen by other writers. However, it goes beyond this. Taking reports, ad campaigns, articles or other written texts and using them without the creator being credited counts as plagiarism.\n<br>\nYou may think that using a few lines written by someone else  is acceptable, or you may say \"What a rotten thing to do!\" The act of stealing work from another writer, whether it is two sentences or an entire essay, has ethical and legal implications.", "id": 2, "time": "24000"}, {"image": "engenn10le12ob07re2img02.jpg", "text": "To be caught plagiarizing copyrighted material is an offence that has consequences, such as heavy fines. It's not always just text either. Let's take a software program for example.  A detailed list of code is included in every program. You may not think much of that, but it may have taken years for a computer program to be perfected. Using anything that is part of a proprietary software being protected by copyright laws is also against the law.\n<br>\n\u201cWhat about art?\u201d you may ask.  Being inspired and influenced by art that you admire, you may accidentally steal an artist's idea. For a new design to be created, a lot of inspiration is required. If you mimic a design that is close to an original work, you may have  unknowingly crossed the divide between influenced and copycat.", "id": 3, "time": "57000"}]}}], "_data": []}], "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "So Much to Do at Work", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Business Ethics", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 12, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Discuss factual and abstract information about common everyday or job related topics in both work and social contexts appropriate for the interlocutor.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "plagiarism", "type": "name"}, {"content": "using another person's words, ideas, or work and pretending it is your own", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This work \"borrowing\" is also known as plagiarism.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use when talking about business ethics.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ad campaign ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a series of advertisements intended to achieve a particular result relating to business", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Their idea for the ad campaign was stolen by the competition.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "creator", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who made a particular thing", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The are the creators of this program.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "credit", "type": "name"}, {"content": "praise that you give to someone for something they have done", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The creators of the program were not given any credit. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to count ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be considered in a particular way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Not giving the creator credit counts as plagiarism. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "copyrighted", "type": "name"}, {"content": "protected by copyright", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Being caught plagiarizing copyrighted work can lead to fines. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "proprietary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to who owns something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Using an image to promote your program or anything that is part of a proprietary software which is being protected by copyright laws is also against the law. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to mimic ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to copy the way someone does something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you mimic a design that is close to an original work, you may have unknowingly crossed the line.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "influenced", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be affected by someone or something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Being inspired and influenced by art that you admire, you may accidentally steal an artist's idea. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob07aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le12ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Passive Infinitives and Gerunds", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the passive infinitive or -ing form in some constructions using the passive voice. <br/>  You use the passive voice when you want to focus on the receiver of the action, rather than the doer (agent).", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "If the subject is not the agent, you use a <span class=\"underline\">passive infinitive</span>:<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">The systems are <span class=\"strong\">to be checked</span> as soon as possible. </span><br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"underline\">passive -ing forms</span> after verbs that are normally followed by a gerund (love, recall etc.)<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">love being given</span> chocolates!</span><br/><br/>  You can use the passive -ing form with the meaning of \u2018because'. <br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Having been bitten</span> by a dog, I have no love of them.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Being pressured</span> to meet a deadline may cause some employees to borrow and present another person's  thoughts or ideas as their own.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You usually think of plagiarism as writers' stories <span class=\"strong\">having been stolen</span> by other writers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">To be caught</span> plagiarizing copyrighted material is an offence. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Expressing Strong Disapproval", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " In a work environment there may come a time when you do not agree with or approve of a decision that somebody made. There are tactful ways to express your disapproval. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Look at the chart below. It contains a list of phrases or expressions you can use. It ranks them from weak to stronger in meaning: <span class=\"prelo-letter-page-break\"></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Phrase\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I don't think much of that.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The speaker disapproves, but is only slightly bothered by the action. They only mildly agree with others who feel far more strongly that they do.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm utterly appalled/disgusted.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The speaker feels more strongly about an action. These phrases are said immediately after they find out about the action.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I'm dead against that.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The speaker is talking about an action that they do not approve of in general.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It shouldn't be allowed!\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The speaker is stating that they would like people legally stopped from doing an action. They feel the action is wrong. They are also inferring that the action, at the present time, is legal.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"What a rotten/mean thing to do.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The speaker has a very strong negative reaction to an action. This is something that they have only just heard about. The speaker sympathizes with the victim to whom the action was done.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Who do they think they are?<br/>  How do people do  such things?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The speaker feels very strongly that an action was wrong.  They disapprove of both the action and those who did it.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You may wonder, <span class=\"strong\">\"How do people do such things?\" </span> <span class=\"strong\">It shouldn't be allowed</span> and it isn't. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">You may not think much of that</span> but it may have taken a programmer years to perfect. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You might think, <span class=\"strong\">\"What a rotten thing to do!\"</span>", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "What's your opinion about plagiarism? Write down your thoughts about it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go to the library or on the Internet. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do some research. Find evidence from articles that support your opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use your research to write a short response paper (16-20 sentences) about your views on plagiarism.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your response.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share it with a partner. Ask for their opinion.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I form an opinion about an issue related to work.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I identify evidence that helps support my opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about issues related to work.", "type": "text"}]}]}